    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_22becd44b499f1ef4eaacdfc2709cbd77a297227191d70c7bd1f1414b1c3b646",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Derivative-zero location supports a hierarchy of diagnostics: Speiser gives the exact RH-equivalent exclusion of ζ′ zeros left of the critical line, Levinson's method turns zeros in a shrinking right-side strip into a quantifiable loss, and Soundararajan's threshold functions encode a graded proximity distribution that the conditional CUE close-pair calculation models only at leading local scale.",
