      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2513cd522fa717311d7c39548f13b1393a2e2fffa6231f4792b67bd143961c07",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For a close unit-circle pair, the pair contribution to f′/f traces a winding-one model curve. Uniform half-plane control of the remaining-zero logarithmic derivative preserves that winding and hence a unique derivative root in the pair's diameter disk; a residue contour then selects this root analytically in the configuration parameters, licensing the even local power-series expansion used in the density calculation.",
