    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2f7c38e6f229e064a871a2a81dc9beb1090a0298fefda0bc61ef0c4a8d36fc35",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Matching local density by N≈log(T/2π) puts CUE angular gaps and radial derivative-root displacements on scales parallel to zeta vertical gaps and horizontal ζ′ displacements. After the close pair is separated from the remaining-root field in each logarithmic derivative, the rescaled zeta calculation has the same leading implicit form and coefficients as the unitary calculation; the CUE heavy-tail scale then corresponds to the Levinson–Montgomery localization scale.",
