    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e900dfbabfe5916f9ebd8a2fe3c8f0990d4c42621cafd6496999b3b785d0a552",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Conditioning two CUE eigenvalues to coalesce at one changes the law of the remaining eigenvalues by a |Λ(1)|^4 weight. That same conditioned ensemble supports two complementary calculations: characteristic-polynomial ratio averages determine the background coefficients in the derivative-root expansion, while its weighted orthogonal-polynomial kernel has a microscopic Bessel limit giving the collision-conditioned one-level density.",
