    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f3667868f261bd6b98027a9d9b7a3a96c498cc15240f7ec476e889c2202bc1e1",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The close-pair mechanism fixes the dominant s^(1/2) small-distance term but is not a global classification of near-boundary derivative roots: separated-root families contribute only the lower-order C·s scale, while numerical distributions exhibit a persistent second mode across CUE, COE, independent-circle-root, and ζ′ data that the local asymptotic does not explain.",
